# Ridge decode oracle — captured by native/tools/ridge_oracle_capture.py.
# The oracle is llama.cpp on the SAME GGUF, CPU-only (so it can serve beside a GPU
# driver). A provenance mismatch below means the oracle moved: recapture, do not
# compare against a stale fixture. `hidden_stage` says WHICH hidden this is.
#
# How to use it, and why the bar is not a fudge: greedy agreement is only meaningful
# where the decision is decisive. Every recorded pick carries its top-2 margin (nats)
# and the runner-up's id, so a gate checks EQUALITY where margin >= margin_bar and
# MEMBERSHIP of {top1, top2} where it is below — a flat position is a coin flip that fp
# noise can move, and a gate that demands equality there flakes on a correct forward.
# Measured on this prompt: the 1-token prefix is inherently thin (after one token the
# distribution is nearly flat), which is exactly the case the membership rule exists for.
oracle llama-server
